# ILKA master rule

Inspect before modifying. Understand existing architecture. Make the smallest safe change. Follow existing conventions. Avoid unnecessary dependencies.

Never expose secrets. Never break existing APIs without a migration plan. Write or update tests. Run relevant tests. Review the git diff. Check for regressions. Update documentation when required.

Never make destructive production changes. Ask for human approval before irreversible actions (schema apply to production, branch deletion, database drops, force-push, file-tree deletion).

Agents must not: delete the repository, reset Git history, drop/truncate databases, modify production data, expose secrets, merge to `main`, or deploy production.

Do not invent application code, schemas, or live telemetry. Label any synthetic data `[MOCK / SYNTHETIC]`. Application code is **SCAFFOLDED** only until Phase 1 starts.

Never silently change architecture (new service, new SoR, Redis) without an ADR. Never remove functionality without justification.

Source of truth: `AGENTS.md`, `CODEX.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `docs/README.md`.
